TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan / Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Table 2: Planned information sources"},{"id":"R6","met":"yes","where":"Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The causal link from ocean acidification to coral bleaching is oversimplified; bleaching is mainly driven by thermal stress, so the cited acidity statement does not support the claim as written."},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","issue":"Hand calculations are sound (period 5,801 s, 97.8° sun-synchronous inclination, 24.2° track shift), but the equations for nodal precession and the ground-track shift are not shown, so the inclination and shift values cannot be verified by the reader."},{"where":"Project Plan","issue":"Launch specifics are scheduled and launch is named in the course material requirement, but no launch vehicle, site or injection analysis is presented, so the launch aspect of R2 is only partly addressed."},{"where":"References","issue":"Reference [4] is a news article used to support a specific technical method (Asner's seafloor colour mapping), rather than the primary publication."}],"overall":"A strong, well-structured preliminary report with a clear, measurable mission concept, a credible Gantt-based plan with contingencies, and correct orbit hand calculations that expose a real coverage trade-off. Weaknesses are the thin launch analysis (R2), some unshown equations, an oversimplified acidification claim, and minor language and length issues. Level marks are scaled from the 10-point descriptors to each criterion's weight.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":10.0,"scale":10.0,"points":40.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"Goal, four measurable objectives, and named users with needs are clearly stated and linked to objectives. Literature is cited throughout. Minor weaknesses: the acidification-to-bleaching causal claim is oversimplified, and a few requirements (e.g. 10 m GSD) are only provisional. Rubric level descriptors are on a 10-point scale; mark scaled to the 40-point weight.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Mission goal. Give reef managers direct, repeatable observations of coral colour over the whole Great Barrier Reef"},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Users and their needs. The satellite would be operated by the Australian Institute of Marine Science (AIMS)."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Accomplished","mark":10.0,"scale":10.0,"points":30.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"Gantt chart with task descriptions, logical ordering justified by the mission narrative, a risk table with triggers and responses, and planned information sources with purposes. Feasibility is convincing. Slightly less detail on week-by-week deliverables and some sources are generic. Scaled to 30-point weight.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"the imaging requirements (objectives 1 and 2) fix the orbit altitude and local time, so orbit work comes before ground control"},{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"Contingencies. Week 10 is float as well as editing time"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Accomplished","mark":9.0,"scale":10.0,"points":9.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Hand calculations for period, orbits per day, sun-synchronous inclination and ground-track shift are correct and checked against STK. Interpretation identifies a real swath-versus-resolution conflict that drives the orbit trade. Results are on track, though the STK outputs themselves are not shown.","evidence":[{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"Swath at 10 m sampling | 10 m × 6,000 pixels across track | 60 km"},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"Weekly coverage (objective 1) is therefore not guaranteed by one satellite at this altitude and resolution."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":10.0,"scale":10.0,"points":20.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Clear headings, labelled figure and tables, and a consistent IEEE-style reference list with in-text citations matching. Weaknesses: some awkward phrasing, a colloquial sentence, reliance on a news article for a key claim, and the length likely exceeds the 2–3 page guideline. Scaled to 20-point weight; placed at the upper Adequate/lower Accomplished boundary.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"but this is not even the full extent of their nurture"},{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"Completed stages are gold. Incomplete stages are blue."}]}]}
